('62077ea0-552b-4905-b977-30b300e9fe85', 'Lateral Raise From Back (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your lateral delts with the Dumbbell Lateral Raise From Back, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '104561201', '104561201-Dumbbell-Lateral-Raise-from-Back-(male)_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lateral Raise From Back. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lateral Raise From Back', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('62198908-a7fd-4c46-8d13-44a8329f0cfc', 'Seated Neck Tap', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Neck Tap is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '51311201', '51311201-Seated-Neck-Tap-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Neck Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'neck_exercise', 'Seated Neck Tap', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('622599d2-2680-4077-bce3-fc6c4c2e9ba5', 'Lying Lower Back Knee To Chest', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your lower back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '72181201', '72181201-Lying-Lower-Back-Knee-to-Chest-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Lower Back Knee To Chest. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Lower Back Knee To Chest. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Lying Lower Back Knee To Chest', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6228674b-20a2-4987-8366-d83b39c3c750', 'Diagonal Opens', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this movement movement that develops pressing power. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '52831201', '52831201-Diagonal-Opens-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Diagonal Opens. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Diagonal Opens', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62333849-7267-40c4-8886-26562983487d', 'Low Lunge (left)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this lunging stretch that helps restore range of motion. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '60091201', '60091201-Low-Lunge-(left)-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Low Lunge. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 6. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Low Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6240fc82-f990-4e73-89af-d52c62ed9234', 'Drag Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '30271201', '30271201-Barbell-Drag-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Drag Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, 'Underhand (Supinated)', 'Standard', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Drag Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('624e029a-db6b-4b5f-9351-28de7eda584a', 'Side Bend Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity lunging exercise that challenges your entire body. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '77021201', '77021201-Side-Bend-Side-Lunge-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend Side Lunge', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6254283f-e17a-4c86-89b5-2edc9c28dffd', 'Frog', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '75941201', '75941201-Frog-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Frog. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Frog', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62592600-e46f-4997-baf3-cbb5cea032f3', 'Low Seated Row With V Bar (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your biceps, lats work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '60321201', '60321201-Cable-Low-Seated-Row-with-V-bar-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the lowest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Low Seated Row With V Bar', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('625bf070-4fe4-44d9-8c33-91e73469dbcd', 'Assisted Tricep Pushdown (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Machine', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Lever Assisted Triceps Pushdown targets your triceps through a pushing motion. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '79301201', '79301201-Lever-Assisted-Triceps-Pushdown-(female)_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Assisted Triceps Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lever Assisted Triceps Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Lever Assisted Triceps Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6264062f-6121-4ef6-80df-9bd3420fc127', 'Lying Floor Negative Half Dragon Flag', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '93191201', '93191201-Lying-Floor-Negative-Half-Dragon-Flag_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Lying Floor Negative Half Dragon Flag. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Floor Negative Half Dragon Flag. 3. Focus on a slow, controlled lowering phase (3-5 seconds). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Lying Floor Negative Half Dragon Flag', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('626e8cd7-84c0-4400-b506-0408eb30ee89', 'Hip Hurdles Over The Bar (Hurdles)', 'Legs', 'Hurdles', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Hip Hurdles Over The Bar is a lower body movement exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '103501201', '103501201-Hip-Hurdles-over-the-Bar-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Hip Hurdles Over The Bar. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Hip Hurdles Over The Bar', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6270c161-2e51-4ccb-a427-0a48e152d5ad', 'Kneeling Fist Roll', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Fist Roll is an arm movement exercise targeting your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '69761201', '69761201-Kneeling-Fist-Roll-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Fist Roll. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Kneeling Fist Roll', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6273bcff-3182-4f14-9023-21a8c2ce780a', 'Hands Behind Head Romanian Deadlift', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this hip hinge exercise. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '95351201', '95351201-Bodyweight-Hands-Behind-Head-Romanian-Deadlift-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Push your hips back, lowering the weight along your legs with a flat back. 2. Lower until you feel a stretch in your hamstrings. 3. Drive hips forward to stand, squeezing glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Hands Behind Head Romanian Deadlift', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62835f34-72ea-4d49-b74d-4c8444c41cee', 'Ski Runners', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Ski Runners is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '55391201', '55391201-Ski-Runners-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Ski Runners. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Ski Runners', 'cycling, rowing_cardio, jump_rope', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('628ad027-c82e-4a63-9b2b-66e636501ec5', 'Bent Over Rear Lateral Raise (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your rear delts. Bending over allows gravity to provide resistance in a different plane. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '8931201', '08931201-Band-bent-over-rear-lateral-raise-(female)_Shoulders.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Bent Over Rear Lateral Raise. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Bent Over Rear Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('628c6a3a-3f30-4c2f-b049-14fe81df12ee', 'Weighted Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Weighted Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '104291201', '104291201-Weighted-Lying-Leg-Raise-Flat-Bench_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Use a flat bench for this exercise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Weighted Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Weighted Lying Leg Raise Flat Bench', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('628e4924-5ef3-499c-8713-352d92b08cc5', 'Standing Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '32531201', '32531201-Standing-Side-Bend-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('628fed0a-787e-446d-a376-b87c9e79af84', 'Chest Fly Side Step', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Chest Fly Side Step is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic flying movements. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '72691201', '72691201-Chest-Fly-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Chest Fly Side Step', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62a95aa7-f111-48a8-a061-e8b66aeeabb1', 'Pullover (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Pullover On Exercise Ball is a pulling exercise that targets your chest muscles. Secondary activation of your lats, triceps provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '12951201', '12951201-Dumbbell-Pullover-on-Exercise-Ball_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Pullover On Exercise Ball. 2. With arms slightly bent, lower the weight behind your head in an arc. 3. Pull the weight back over your chest, squeezing your lats and chest. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pullover', 'Pullover On Exercise Ball', 'bicep_curl, face_pull, lat_pulldown', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('62ca29eb-75b5-48d2-b537-64b9f00719cc', 'Seated Single Straight Back Hamstring Lean (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Seated Single Straight Back Hamstring Lean is a movement exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '94561201', '94561201-Sitting-Single-Straight-Back-Hamstring-Lean-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Single Straight Back Hamstring Lean. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 38, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Single Straight Back Hamstring Lean', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('62cb8992-1fbb-47c5-b431-aecc74691acd', 'Captains Chair Straight Leg Raise (Roman Chair)', 'Core', 'Roman Chair, Chair', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Captains Chair Straight Leg Raise, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '46141201', '46141201-Captains-Chair-Straight-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.166461+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 3. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Captains Chair Straight Leg Raise', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62d93c26-1f46-4ed8-8544-aa429cee1f35', 'Triceps Press Bench Supported (Flat Bench)', 'Arms', 'Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Triceps Press Bench Supported targets your triceps through a pressing motion. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '104041201', '104041201-Triceps-Press-Bench-Supported-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Triceps Press Bench Supported', 'bench_press, chest_fly, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62dcfd90-44df-40b3-ad0a-eac5298b927e', 'Opposite Arm Raise (Against Wall)', 'Shoulders', 'Wall', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this raising movement focusing on your core. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '93621201', '93621201-Opposite-Arm-Raise-against-Wall-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Opposite Arm Raise Against Wall. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Opposite Arm Raise Against Wall', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62e62a56-8de9-478c-83cc-c96829a8d68e', 'Jump Squat (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '11171201', '11171201-Suspender-Jump-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Jump Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Explode upward from the bottom, jumping as high as possible. 5. Land softly with bent knees and immediately descend into the next rep. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 75, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Suspender Jump Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('62f64340-ee84-4f4c-9b9b-4b23069b6305', 'Standing Under Knee Clap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Under Knee Clap builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '85071201', '85071201-Standing-Under-Knee-Clap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Under Knee Clap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Under Knee Clap', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62f9ccb6-8871-401e-a083-1ca980eef0c1', '45 Degrees Back Extension Scapular Adduction (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The 45 Degrees Back Extension Scapular Adduction strengthens your lower back muscles through a controlled extension motion. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '88951201', '88951201-45-degrees-Back-Extension-Scapular-Adduction-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', '45 Degrees Back Extension Scapular Adduction', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('62fb0674-7729-4af3-999e-f38fc9862ff5', 'Battling Ropes', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop functional strength with the Battling Ropes, a comprehensive movement exercise. Secondary activation of your shoulders, core provides additional muscle engagement. Compound movements like this develop coordination, power, and overall fitness.', '1281201', '01281201-Battling-Ropes.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Battling Ropes. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Battling Ropes', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('630a2bb9-679b-4720-8206-f730e381bd90', 'Walking Circle Draw', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '99181201', '99181201-Walking-Circle-Draw-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking Circle Draw. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Circle Draw', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63291606-e21f-4c26-892b-8e48540b0876', 'Bow Yoga Pose_back', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your back, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '14811201', '14811201-Bow-Yoga-Pose_Back_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.847006+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Bow Yoga Pose_back. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Bow Yoga Pose_back', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('633c1741-a1da-4d22-801a-1da6117658c8', 'Seated Calf Raise (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Calf Raise (plate Loaded) isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '31061201', '31061201-Lever-Seated-Calf-Raise-(plate-loaded)-(female)_Calves.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Calf Raise. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Seated Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, standing_calf_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('6341fac7-2263-48f4-ad3a-b9b0284a20b9', 'Seated External Shoulder Rotation (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your rotator cuff with the Seated External Shoulder Rotation On Chair, an effective shoulder rotation exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '104931201', '104931201-Seated-External-Shoulder-Rotation-on-Chair-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Seated External Shoulder Rotation On Chair. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated External Shoulder Rotation On Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('634759b2-7e13-490b-904c-3feac3072670', 'Preacher Curl (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell, Preacher Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '701201', '00701201-Barbell-Preacher-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Isolation', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, 'Underhand (Supinated)', 'Standard', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('63572277-1013-44e4-bbf0-d5bae8a4df43', 'Lotus Yoga Pose Padmasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lotus Yoga Pose Padmasana is a flexibility exercise that targets your hips, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Secondary activation of your adductors provides additional muscle engagement. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '9561201', '09561201-Lotus-Yoga-Pose-Padmasana-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Lotus Yoga Pose Padmasana. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Lotus Yoga Pose Padmasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('636f9083-c2cc-4cc0-a2af-bcf22d299b19', 'Lying Leg Over Knee Hip Twist Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85641201', '85641201-Lying-Leg-Over-Knee-Hip-Twist-Stretch-(female)_Str.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Over Knee Hip Twist Stretch. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Lying Leg Over Knee Hip Twist Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Lying Leg Over Knee Hip Twist Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63ab4e5f-4abf-416e-b016-cfc9ba03aabc', 'Lying Leg Hang Abductor Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lying Leg Hang Abductor Stretch is a lower body stretching exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '18841201', '18841201-Lying-Leg-Hang-Abductor-Stretch_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Leg Hang Abductor Stretch. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lying Leg Hang Abductor Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Lying Leg Hang Abductor Stretch', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63ae1de4-fe13-48e0-81c8-1612660b0d6f', 'Overhead Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57241201', '57241201-Dumbbell-Overhead-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Overhead Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Overhead Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('63ae840e-ac3e-47ef-ac45-0fae38de015e', 'Cross Lat Pulldown (Machine, Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Lever Cross Lat Pulldown builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The shoulders, core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '68811201', '68811201-Lever-Cross-Lat-Pulldown-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Cross Lat Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Lever Cross Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('63c4926a-2959-42b0-8a34-2e00f2561a86', 'Single Arm Low Chest Fly (Resistance Band)', 'Chest', 'Resistance Band', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Resistance Band Single Arm Low Chest Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '91381201', '91381201-Resistance-Band-Single-Arm-Low-Chest-Fly-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Single Arm Low Chest Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Single Arm Low Chest Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('63cfb431-e4ac-44e8-9c47-7ac2e2a1a8ff', 'Body Up', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This movement movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Secondary activation of your chest provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '1371201', '01371201-Body-Up_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Body Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Body Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63d00cdf-89d7-43c4-9677-5c8a38aa21e8', 'Squat Power Pull (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this pulling exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '72791201', '72791201-Suspender-Squat-Power-Pull-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Squat Power Pull. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Perform the concentric (lifting) phase explosively with maximum effort. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Suspender Squat Power Pull', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('63d1e814-935b-46ed-b457-14226efeba5a', 'Crunch (arms Straight)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '2661201', '02661201-Crunch-(arms-straight)_waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Great for building strength in your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63d88440-48b7-4124-ad9f-66bbb9747020', 'Jump Step Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Jump Step Jump is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic jumping movements. You''ll also feel your quads, calves working to support the movement. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '47061201', '47061201-Jump-Step-Jump_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Jump Step Jump. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Jump Step Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('63df4333-76b2-435b-9e28-f945260d86a2', 'Farmers Carry (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Core","Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your forearms. Your traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '29171201', '29171201-Dumbbell-Farmers-Carry_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.991486+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Farmers Carry. 2. Set up in the starting position for Dumbbell Farmers Carry. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Farmers Carry', 'deadlift, shrug, suitcase_carry', TRUE, 'dumbbell', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('63fa96ee-1ec0-40ec-98a2-4c4926d7d3e7', 'Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor (Kettlebell)', 'Chest', 'Kettlebell', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your chest for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '100241201', '100241201-Kettlebell-Lying-Straight-Arm-Press-on-Floor-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Kettlebell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 3. Lie down in the appropriate position for Kettlebell Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor. 4. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 5. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 6. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Lying Straight Arm Press On Floor', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('63fd431b-f9a5-45e4-865b-58d44d95bdb6', 'Leaning Forward Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this lunging exercise for quad development. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '90781201', '90781201-Leaning-Forward-Side-Lunge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Leaning Forward Side Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6402ca75-a63f-44d6-bd79-56916ffcc0d7', 'Behind The Back Cuffed Lateral Raise (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Cable Behind The Back Cuffed Lateral Raise is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '104091201', '104091201-Cable-Behind-The-Back-Cuffed-Lateral-Raise-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Behind The Back Cuffed Lateral Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Behind The Back Cuffed Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('6424101e-4424-4698-a950-6832c8bd8c2e', 'Ring Leg Curl With Yoga Block (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings, Yoga Block', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. The calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '77081201', '77081201-Ring-Leg-Curl-with-yoga-block_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 2. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 3. Extend legs back out with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Ring Leg Curl With Yoga Block', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('6425c4c2-e887-4ce9-a516-446887a6ff03', 'Ab Coaster Crunch (Machine)', 'Core', 'Machine', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lever Ab Coaster Crunch, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '55831201', '55831201-Lever-Ab-Coaster-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Ab Coaster Crunch. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lever Ab Coaster Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('642a7928-aca3-4ade-9a41-723ed6f41f90', 'Side Plank Single Knee Drive', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '76701201', '76701201-Side-Plank-Single-Knee-Drive-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Side Plank Single Knee Drive', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6433c45f-463b-49ec-93f0-249f90b330e3', 'Pulldown - Underhand (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Underhand Pulldown is a pulling exercise that targets your latissimus dorsi for a wider back. The biceps, upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '2451201', '02451201-Cable-Underhand-Pulldown_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Underhand Pulldown. 2. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Underhand Pulldown', 'Pulldown - Underhand', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('64350610-2361-4c77-9abc-7eaf09cfdd2c', 'Push Up (On Knees)', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '11821201', '11821201-Push-up-(on-knees)-(female)_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Great for building strength in your chest.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('6440e8a9-1bae-446c-9501-7bf2f2f91cee', 'Wipers (Straight Leg)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Wipers (straight Leg), focusing on your abs. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '70091201', '70091201-Wipers-(straight-leg)-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wipers. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Wipers', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('644793db-3383-48c0-9e92-35003704f19e', 'Shrug (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this shrugging movement targeting your traps. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '2201201', '02201201-Cable-Shrug_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.397686+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('64506a1e-609d-41b0-b6ed-06c2bc987288', 'Seated Stick Pass Around Stretch', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Seated Stick Pass Around Stretch is a stretching exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '89451201', '89451201-Seated-Stick-Pass-Around-Stretch-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.698781+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Stick Pass Around Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Stick Pass Around Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65);
